Chapter 3
Horizontal Analysis and the Base Year
التحليل الأفقي وسنة الأساس
A common-size column tells you what a company is made of. It cannot tell you what has changed, because each year is divided by its own total and a line that grew exactly as fast as the company shows no movement at all. You saw that in Chapter 2: Orontes's current liabilities rose by $710,000 and stayed at 13.5 per cent of total assets both years.
Horizontal analysis is the other direction. Each line is compared with the same line in an earlier year, so the question becomes what moved and by how much. Because the comparison runs across the page, it is horizontal; the common-size comparison runs down the column, so it is vertical.
Figure F503-01 is your map.
Figure F503-01. Chapter 3 roadmap: one line, two years, three ways of stating the difference.
