3.3  Horizontal analysis of the income statement
A balance sheet comes with one comparative. An income statement is usually shown for three years, and three years is the minimum from which an analyst will read a direction. Figure F503-05 is Orontes's.
Figure F503-05. Orontes Foods, Inc. — income statement, three years (whole USD)
@table
Line | 2025 | 2024 | 2023
Net sales | 42,000,000 | 36,400,000 | 32,000,000
Cost of goods sold | (27,300,000) | (23,296,000) | (20,160,000)
Gross profit | 14,700,000 | 13,104,000 | 11,840,000
Total operating expenses | (10,524,000) | (9,100,000) | (8,320,000)
Operating income | 4,176,000 | 4,004,000 | 3,520,000
Net income | 2,969,100 | 2,598,000 | 2,320,000
@end
Figure F503-06 turns it into year-over-year percentages and into an index on a 2023 base.
Figure F503-06. Orontes Foods, Inc. — income statement trends
@table
Line | 2024 change | 2025 change | Index 2023 = 100, at 2025
Net sales | 13.8 | 15.4 | 131.2
Cost of goods sold | 15.6 | 17.2 | 135.4
Gross profit | 10.7 | 12.2 | 124.2
Total operating expenses | 9.4 | 15.6 | 126.5
Operating income | 13.8 | 4.3 | 118.6
Net income | 12.0 | 14.3 | 128.0
@end
Now the statement speaks. Sales grew 13.8 per cent and then 15.4 per cent: a company accelerating. But cost of goods sold grew faster in both years, 15.6 and then 17.2 per cent, so gross profit grew more slowly than sales. That is the whole story of the common-size margin falling from 37.0 per cent in 2023 to 36.0 and then 35.0 per cent.
Operating income grew 13.8 per cent in 2024 and only 4.3 per cent in 2025, far slower than sales. The reason is in the operating expenses, which rose 15.6 per cent in 2025 — and most of that rise is the impairment. Take the impairment out and the picture changes completely, which is why Chapter 17 insists on identifying lines that do not recur before any trend is read.
EXAM TRAP   Read the lines against each other
A cost growing faster than sales means a falling margin, every time. You do not need the common-size statement to see it.
A subtotal growing more slowly than the line above it means something between them grew faster.
When one year breaks a trend, find the line that broke it before explaining the trend.
LANGUAGE FOCUS   "Trend" and "tendency"
English trend means the direction of a series over time, and it carries no judgment: a trend can be bad. Arabic اتجاه and French tendance are the same. What English does not allow is using trend of a single movement between two points. Two numbers give a change; three or more give a trend.
